  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: If adding the boiled eggs, bring a small saucepan of water to the boil. Halve the tomato, then thinly slice. Trim the lettuce, then separate the leaves. Peel the cucumber into ribbons with a vegetable peeler. Slice the haloumi.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2287090/photos/large/283943_1-8158fcf9a89688f5d7cbbb3a5f56de86.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast almonds: Cook 2 eggs in the pan of boiling water for 6 mins for soft-boiled, or 8 mins for hard-boiled. Drain, then cool in cold water. Meanwhile, cook the almonds in a cold medium frypan over medium heat, tossing, for 3-4 mins until toasted. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2287091/photos/large/283943_2-850f5fbc8cd6dd7c50e02cbe4a9f9753.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook haloumi: Heat 2 tsp olive oil in the same pan over medium-high heat. Scatter ½ tsp oregano over the haloumi then cook for 2 mins each side or until golden. Remove the haloumi from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2287092/photos/large/283943_3-2c58eb29d3998115e8ac9b804a063ea5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make salad: Put the tomato, lettuce, cucumber and green goddess dressing in a bowl, season with salt and pepper and toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2287093/photos/large/283943_4-67748553711fa9d215a8955141720ff9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Peel and quarter the eggs. Divide the salad, haloumi and eggs among bowls. Scatter with the almonds and a pinch of oregano. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2287094/photos/large/283943_5-5ee6b0c70f3ef80250ea13bfc891742f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Haloumi is a brined, slightly springy cheese originally from Cyprus. Traditionally it was made from a mixture of goat and sheep milk, although these days cow's milk is also used. The haloumi we use is made using vegetable rennet, so it's suitable for vegetarians.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2287095/photos/large/283943_6-6008943387a372362a097cc2b5e7fe2e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
